EL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-receiver-action-mismatch</code> |\n12330|| logs | receiver | cursor-projection | explicit --peer host with cursor | destination_host_id | equals peer_host per-endpoint | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-receiver-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12331|| logs | both | initial-projection | route logs | action | both equal logs | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-both-action-mismatch</code> |\n12332|| logs | both | initial-projection | explicit --peer host | destination_host_id | both equal peer_host | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-projection-both-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12333|| logs | both | cursor-projection | route logs with cursor | action | both equal logs | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-both-action-mismatch</code> |\n12334|| logs | both | cursor-projection | explicit --peer host with cursor | destination_host_id | both equal peer_host | <code>SEL-CASE-logs-cursor-projection-both-destination-mismatch</code> |\n12335|\n12336|Other managed-session remote action routes use Section 11's existing typed\n12337|session_id and LeaseExpectation/transaction IDs; they MUST carry the selected\n12338|UUID and existing expected authority, never convert either into a CLI NAME.\n12339|Their closed RPC envelopes and bound error versions are unchanged. Selector\n12340|failures are emitted locally as CLI5/Error1.4, not inserted into an older RPC.\n12341|\n12342|#### 14.7.3 Authoritative summaries and closed failure binding\n12343|\n12344|Selector-capable CLI defaults to CLI Result 5.0.0 and Structured Error 1.4.0.\n12345|Explicit <code>--result-version VERSION</code> selects a supported exact CLI\n12346|Result version before parsing command operands; unsupported versions fail locally\n12347|with incompatible_schema. Version 5 retains the exact v4 success envelope,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
