{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caa3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a087bb-8c16-7c41-9df2-bf65e2d2e1e6"},"sequence":940,"recorded_at":1780531400001875,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a5a4bafa-7c8c-485e-ade1-b2a300d515d9","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"a5a4bafa-7c8c-485e-ade1-b2a300d515d9","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a5a4bafa-7c8c-485e-ade1-b2a300d515d9"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a087c2-b001-7791-9f1a-049002fce81e"},"task_id":"01a087c2-b001-7791-9f1a-049002fce81e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a087c2-b001-7791-9f1a-049002fce81e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-27-1\",\n  \"command\": \"bash -c 'grep -n \\\"lease_record_id\\\" README.md internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md | head; echo ===; grep -n \\\"Two members\\\\|One member\\\" -r internal/ README.md 2>/dev/null | head; echo ===; head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md'\",\n  \"description\": \"Check docs for stale member-count claims\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md:96:- `lease_record_id` is unbound: this stack carries no Lease Record\\n===\\ninternal/canonicaljson/testdata/array-order-constraints.md:96:| `closed_shapes.go` | `validateWorkspaceSnapshot` | `members` | Two members with an equal `workspace_id` are refused. Section 10.1 declares only \\\"in workspace-ID order\\\"; the one-for-one correspondence it names is with the Workspace Group Record, whose own member ordering declares no `workspace_id` uniqueness either. | TASK-260830-uqnwmi |\\ninternal/sessquery/plan.go:14:// One member of the sixteen-row contract table stays unbound in this\\n===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-09\\n\\n### TASK-260908-2tkufa: recovered v0.6.0 consumer adoption and bound pending runtime owners\\n- AUTHORITY: catalogue generation, Current, CI roots and traceability consume the adopted v0.6.0 lock/document/inventory; three release projections preserve V050/V043 history. Metadata digest `5788d45d…87b963`; ownership digest `a1ab2913…f3b130d`. Localstore explicitly calls CurrentV050. Error 1.4 remains census-only; no new runtime capability is claimed.\\n- RECOVERY: prior CR1 failed command 21 because task-board.config.json still passed v0.5.0 inputs to the strict v0.6.0 generator. Changed only that command in candidate and authorized control root; control-root pre-existing config diff was empty and both complete config files now match. TestConfiguredCRCatalogGateConsumesAdoptedAuthority drives the configured command through cataloggen.run and refuses stale authority. No model, signing, required gate or hosted-trigger policy changed.\\n- OWNERS: all 13 new headings name pending task owners; the source-derived TestAdoptedSectionsHavePendingOwnersAndRefuseRuntimeAdmission requires 13/13 and refuses each through VerifyAssignedSections. TASK-260909-2ez769 owns credentials/trust lifecycle and Config-4 migration; existing selector, RPC admission, CLI, lifecycle, conformance and negotiation owners retain their old AC and explicit historical scope. Board dependencies preserve the signed-Story landing barrier. Detailed responsibility split: internal/traceability/adoption-v0.6.0.md. No other Story partial implementation was edited.\\n- CORRECTION: sections 11.10.5 and 14.7.5 own upstream synthetic publication evaluators, not runtime SPEC.md policy readers. Their product conformance consumers are named without calling source evidence runtime support. Removed the predecessor's assessment-only Config-4 production expansion: catalogue census does not justify accepting an unimplemented reader. The version-pair test now proves 6 read-only, 6 compatible and 4 refused-reader cases; Config-4 Load and Migrate refusal remains explicit. No config production code changes remain.\\n- EVIDENCE: all 26 configured local gates passed; later focused config rework passed and the final handoff reruns the same gates on its captured candidate. Eleven narrowing mutants each produced semantic assertion failures with 11 passing instrumentation controls; token-preserving stale generator directive still passes the static token check and fails the behavioral CLI suite. Mutations ran in a task-scoped copy and were restored byte-exact. One initial M4 applicator failed because instrumentation split its exact needle; that attempt is recorded as setup failure, not a kill, and the corrected battery re-proved all rows. Archived per-command exits supersede the prior unarchived battery claims.\\n- FIGURES: contracts=63, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=101, fixtures=32, historical contracts=55; bindings=56 (full=1, partial=3, sliver=1, unevidenced=48, unmeasured=3), unowned=12, discharged clauses=17/463. README's stale 53/428 sample was corrected. The 17 existing discharges are preserved; no new runtime clause is claimed.\\n- HANDOFF: uncommitted candidate at signed checkpoint b4c43495; developer handoff publishes a reviewable task-board CR. Independent review and signed Story landing remain orchestrator-owned, and dependent owners remain blocked on landing. This entry does not claim review acceptance or delivery.\\n\\n### TASK-260908-3kvnm2: adopted signed v0.6.0 normative source alongside v0.5.0, no consumer re-pointed\\n- PROVENANCE (verified this session, upstream read-only): `verify-tag v0.6.0` exit 0 (tag object `40c123eb…861a785`, ECDSA `SHA256:V6JiKG7J29mjsvikcLoSVp0bLa77VTsFy12gnLO81cM`), peeled commit `0cbdf100…67859a6` (`verify-commit` exit 0, `ls-remote` peeled ref equal), SPEC.md 1150005 bytes SHA256 `74504539…90896b` measured from the tagged blob. Delivery is the signed git tag; no hosted GitHub Release exists (release-verdict archive), so only immutable commit/blob URLs are referenced.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/specpin/{pin,sections}.go` + `v0.6.0.lock.json` (63 contracts, 5 fixtures), `internal/specdoc/{specdoc.go,SPEC.v0.6.0.md}` + `pin060_test.go`, `sections060_test.go`, `specdoc060_test.go`, README provenance paragraphs. `v0.5.0.lock.json`, `SPEC.md`, `Current`/`Verify`/`Load`/`Parse` and all existing tests byte-untouched in behavior.\\n- DELTA (measured, SPEC §1.5 cross-checked row-for-row in order): +Session selector `urn:ax:contract:session-selector` 1.0.0, +Host Channel `urn:ax:transport:host-channel` 1.0.0, +Host Trust Store 1.0.0; Configuration +4.0.0, Mesh RPC +5.0.0, Structured error +1.4.0, CLI result +5.0.0; +13 sections (6.6, 11.10.x6, 14.7.x6), normative scope still 24; +2 fixtures (host-channel `20aa66c3…`, selector `2bda47f5…`), 3 old fixture files byte-identical upstream. Selector fixture ID is pin-local (`ax-session-selector-conformance-v1`, path-stem convention — upstream file carries `specification_version`/`contract`, no `fixture` discriminator); host-channel ID matches the upstream discriminator.\\n- HISTORY: v0.6.0 projections of v0.5.0 (60 rows) and v0.4.3 (55 rows) are `reflect.DeepEqual` to the real v0.5.0 lock and its projection — adoption cannot rewrite history. `ContractsForRelease(v0.6.0)` on a v0.5.0 manifest is refused: a stale pin cannot authorize the new release. New runtime contracts (selector/auth) are pinned only; no `ax` surface claims them.\\n- MUTANTS (4 narrowing, each admits exactly one member, each kills exactly its named subtest, full suites otherwise green, all restored cmp-clean): M1 digest+trailing-newline, M2 identity+stale-commit (v0.6.0 tokens preserved), M3 ParseV060+stale-v0.5.0-doc, M4 token-preserving delta-row Versions drop. Detail in `.temp/TASK-260908-3kvnm2/mutant-results.md`.\\n- DEPENDENCY: catalogue/traceability regeneration is sibling TASK-260908-2tkufa, after this leaf checkpoints. `Current`/`Verify`/`Load` intentionally still serve v0.5.0 until then.\\n- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n## 2026-09-08\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1r9wrr: missing Type-ownership gate before R2-F2 rework\\n- FINDING: rev2 recognized only direct-selector dispatch. PB (copy then switch) and PC (string helper) preserved every searched token, compiled, and survived while Reduce applied an unknown-v1 lifecycle effect. PA was census-only; the earlier behavioral label was wrong and is corrected below.\\n- GATE FIRST: all production Type selector uses now derive through invcore into an exact AST-context ownership ledger. Copies, arguments, pointers, closures, package bindings, writes and unclassified contexts are refused at the read/use boundary; unregistered/orphan/duplicate checks are control-planted. The four existing uses remain unchanged. The event-spelling census is composed with this prerequisite, not described as a dataflow analysis.\\n- LIVE EVIDENCE: committed TestCensusLiveEventOwnershipPlants wires PA/PB/PC/PD into Reduce and compiles each. All four are census-only kills; none is called a behavioral kill. Neutral identity control survives; a token-preserving unknown-default lifecycle rewrite fails TestReduceTreatsUnknownV1TypeAsInert. Narrowing the ownership gate to admit only kind := event.Type fails TestCensusLiveEventOwnershipPlants/PB. Separate post-gate control probes prove all four live plants reach the wrong idle state; they do not inflate delivered behavioral coverage. Prerequisite outcome was attached before any broader claim or Local change.\\n- BOUND: direct Type-field access only; no proof of reflective/unsafe/serialization access to whole Event values or later interpretation of diagnostic strings. Other Type selectors are conservatively refused for classification. Parse-only controls and compiling live controls are reported separately.\\n- R2-F2: no product validation invented. With an empty authoritative chain, Local (including malformed and partial tuples) is ignored, LocalHostID derives no role, and a valid Union can still select a winner and its named conflict. TestReduceEmptyChainLocalIsIgnored compares the entire projection with the no-Local baseline, with and without a selected Union winner. README/doc.go now state the exact bound; old F7 closure is narrowed to its Union half.\\n- SCOPE: existing sixteen-path candidate preserved, no manual Story commit or sibling worker; sessrepo/provhost untouched. Verification and separately classified selected battery are attached in the task-scoped rev3 outcome. Independent review and checkpoint remain the orchestrator's responsibility.\\n\\n## 2026-09-07\\n\\n### TASK-260830-1r9wrr rev2: F1/F2/F4/F5/F6 repaired; F3 and F7 Local remained open\\n- SCOPE: same story worktree, still uncommitted (16 CR paths: LOGBOOK, README, 14 files under `internal/sessstate/`). No `internal/sessrepo` or `internal/provhost` file touched.\\n- F1 (`resolveWinner` case 0): the arm cleared `offChainWinner` exactly when the winner was already off-chain, so a duplicated union entry dropped the `union_supersedes_chain` conflict and its warning. Fix: the arm is a documented no-op. Pinned by `TestWinnerResolutionDuplicateOffChainUnionKeepsConflict` plus the triple-copy/losing-branch both-orders `...StaysResolved` (one step past the vector).\\n- F2 (`applyLocalLease`): implemented as not-equal against three sources stating lost-the-tuple. Fix: `>= 0` stands, only `< 0` stales. Pinned by `TestReduceLocalLeaseTupleRule` (equal / greater-epoch / greater-lease-id stand, lesser stales) — the greater-lease-id row exercises the second arm of `Compare`, one step past the reported vector.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 10402,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2601,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
